\b 2 Problem Requirements and Constraints\b0\par
\b 2.1 Functional Requirements\b0\par
The functional requirements of the WASLE platform define the core system behaviors necessary to satisfy the needs of its five primary user roles: customers, merchants, drivers, delivery companies, and pickup point operators. These requirements were identified through stakeholder analysis and system use-case modeling. To ensure clarity and prioritization, the MoSCoW method was applied.\par
\par
The requirements are organized around key system functionalities, including authentication, order lifecycle management, payment handling, real-time communication, remittance workflows, administrative control, and automated delivery assignment. Each requirement contributes to ensuring system reliability, security, and scalability within a multi-role distributed environment.\par
\par
ID\tab Requirement\tab Description\tab Priority\par
FR-01\tab Multi-role registration\tab The system shall support separate registration flows for customers, merchants, drivers, delivery companies, and pickup point applicants, each capturing role-specific profile data.\tab Must Have\par
FR-02\tab OTP email authentication\tab All self-registered users shall authenticate using an 8-digit OTP sent to a verified email address; password-based authentication is not supported for standard user flows.\tab Must Have\par
FR-03\tab Role-based dashboard routing\tab Upon authentication, the system shall route each user to a role-specific dashboard exposing only the functions applicable to that role.\tab Must Have\par
FR-04\tab Merchant order creation\tab Merchants shall create delivery orders specifying customer details, delivery address, COD amount, delivery company, and optionally a pickup point destination.\tab Must Have\par
FR-05\tab Linked payment creation\tab The system shall create a corresponding payment record whenever a new order is created, ensuring that order and payment data remain synchronized.\tab Must Have\par
FR-06\tab Automated driver assignment\tab The system shall automatically assign orders to eligible approved drivers while enforcing same-company ownership, order-state constraints, vehicle-capacity compatibility, and route-based selection.\tab Must Have\par
FR-07\tab Driver verification workflow\tab New drivers shall require approval by a delivery company administrator before accessing operational features.\tab Must Have\par
FR-08\tab Real-time order status updates\tab Authorized stakeholders shall receive real-time updates as the order progresses through its lifecycle states.\tab Must Have\par
FR-09\tab Customer order tracking\tab Customers shall be able to track active orders by viewing their current delivery status and related order information.\tab Must Have\par
FR-10\tab Pickup point application workflow\tab Applicants shall submit a structured pickup point application with verification photographs; the application shall enter a pending, approved, or rejected administrative workflow.\tab Must Have\par
FR-11\tab Online payment initiation\tab The system shall support secure initialization of online customer payments through an external payment provider.\tab Should Have\par
FR-12\tab Real-time payment status updates\tab Customers and authorized operators shall receive updated payment status information without requiring manual page refresh.\tab Should Have\par
FR-13\tab Cash remittance management\tab Pickup point operators shall record and confirm cash-on-delivery payment transmission to the platform through the supported remittance workflow.\tab Must Have\par
FR-14\tab Field-agent fallback collection\tab The system shall support a fallback process in which an authorized field agent confirms physical collection of cash when a pickup point cannot remit digitally.\tab Should Have\par
FR-15\tab Driver location updates\tab The system shall allow active drivers to update their GPS coordinates through the platform for location-aware operations.\tab Should Have\par
FR-16\tab Order and payment audit log\tab The system shall maintain a complete and chronological record of relevant order and payment state transitions accessible to authorized users.\tab Must Have\par
FR-17\tab Order cancellation\tab Merchants shall be able to request cancellation of undelivered orders with a mandatory reason field.\tab Should Have\par
FR-18\tab Driver company request\tab Registered drivers shall submit join requests to delivery companies, and companies shall approve or reject these requests.\tab Must Have\par
FR-19\tab Company driver management\tab Delivery company administrators shall view, approve, and manage their approved driver fleet.\tab Must Have\par
FR-20\tab Agent administration\tab Platform administrators shall be able to create and manage field agent accounts used for fallback cash collection operations.\tab Should Have\par
FR-21\tab Vehicle capacity assignment\tab The system shall assign predefined capacity limits to each driver based on the selected vehicle type, including weight, volume, and item-count constraints.\tab Must Have\par
FR-22\tab Route estimation and fallback\tab The system shall estimate travel duration and distance for assignment decisions using an external routing service, reuse cached route results when available, and apply fallback estimation when the routing service is unavailable.\tab Must Have\par
